{"help": "https://www.envidat.ch/api/3/action/help_show?name=package_show", "success": true, "result": {"author": "[{\"affiliation\": \"WSL\", \"affiliation_02\": \"\", \"affiliation_03\": \"\", \"email\": \"envidat.ch@volkwein.de\", \"given_name\": \"Axel\", \"identifier\": \"0000-0003-3585-6426\", \"name\": \"Volkwein\"}, {\"affiliation\": \"WSL\", \"affiliation_02\": \"\", \"affiliation_03\": \"\", \"email\": \"werner.gerber@wsl.ch\", \"given_name\": \"Werner\", \"identifier\": \"\", \"name\": \"Gerber\"}]", "author_email": null, "creator_user_id": "a00d2097-51c2-4c3e-adec-58fda68a7451", "date": "[{\"date\": \"2014-06-23\", \"date_type\": \"collected\", \"end_date\": \"2014-06-27\"}]", "doi": "10.16904/envidat.34", "funding": "[{\"grant_number\": \"\", \"institution\": \"Funding information not available.\", \"institution_url\": \"\"}]", "id": "6a7664a6-77a9-49c9-9498-4b63c018fa09", "isopen": true, "language": "en", "license_id": "odc-odbl", "license_title": "ODbL with Database Contents License (DbCL)", "license_url": "https://opendefinition.org/licenses/odc-odbl", "maintainer": "{\"affiliation\": \"WSL\", \"email\": \"envidat.ch@volkwein.de\", \"given_name\": \"Axel\", \"identifier\": \"0000-0003-3585-6426\", \"name\": \"Volkwein\"}", "maintainer_email": null, "metadata_created": "2018-03-08T12:36:55.978477", "metadata_modified": "2025-02-13T15:14:09.929063", "name": "tschamut2014", "notes": "In summer 2014, 6 rock blocks between 20 and 80kg have been thrown in total 111 times down a slope at the Swiss Oberalppass close to the village Tschamut. The slope was mainly covered by grass and its lower part was flat and large enough to provide natural runouts of the single trajectories.\r\n\r\nAn extensive measurement program has been set up to measure the block trajectories: With surveyor's instruments the slope and the six used rock blocks were scanned and the start and end positions of each test were recorded. During the single events two cameras filmed the trajectories. A special sensor device located within the blocks recorded the acting accelerations and rotational speeds over time. Further, the device emitted a Wifi signal that got detected from eight receivers around the slope. Based on this signal the block position has been recorded over time. \r\n\r\nThe dataset contains all data that were gathered through above field campaign.", "num_resources": 4, "num_tags": 9, "organization": {"id": "8ca28da8-ad8f-401a-9356-0aa7fdba2604", "name": "gebirgshydrologie", "title": "GebirgsHydrologie", "type": "organization", "description": " The Research Unit investigates natural hazard processes in mountainous areas, in particular the triggering and propagation of floods, sediment transport, landslides, debris flows and rock fall. Process studies on the scale of slopes, channels and catchments form the basis for the development of simulation models and of hazard assessment procedures and for the design of countermeasures. To this end worldwide unique observation systems are developed, such as a debris flow balance and geophone systems for bedload transport. Damage and damaging processes due to frequent and extreme events are assessed as prerequisites for the risk-based and sustainable management of natural hazards.\r\n\r\nA second focus of the unit is on the estimation and prediction of snow and water resources, e.g. for hydropower production or early recognition of drought. The unit operates a snow hydrological service for federal and cantonal agencies and a drought information platform for a broad range of water users.\r\n\r\n__Further information__: https://www.wsl.ch/en/about-wsl/organization/research-units/mountain-hydrology.html", "image_url": "2018-07-10-091052.004438LogoWSL.svg", "created": "2016-09-02T14:17:02.029939", "is_organization": true, "approval_status": "approved", "state": "active"}, "owner_org": "8ca28da8-ad8f-401a-9356-0aa7fdba2604", "private": false, "publication": "{\"publication_year\":\"2018\", \"publisher\": \"EnviDat\"}", "publication_state": "published", "related_datasets": "", "related_publications": "", "resource_type": "dataset", "resource_type_general": "dataset", "spatial": "{\"type\":\"Polygon\",\"coordinates\":[[[8.700474500656126,46.653806330596865],[8.700345754623413,46.653379198033164],[8.70068907737732,46.65264275465613],[8.701697587966919,46.6527163994451],[8.702598810195923,46.65321718135065],[8.702834844589233,46.653600129090734],[8.702040910720825,46.65455748657749],[8.700882196426392,46.65423345978701],[8.700474500656126,46.653806330596865]]]}", "spatial_info": "Switzerland", "state": "active", "subtitle": "", "title": "Repetitive trajectory testing in Tschamut 2014", "type": "dataset", "url": null, "version": "1.0", "extras": [{"key": "dora_link", "value": ""}], "resources": [{"cache_last_updated": null, "cache_url": null, "created": "2018-03-08T12:41:50.157992", "description": "These data contain the point clouds obtained from laser scanning the test slope and the six test blocks used for the experiments. The coordinates of the slope are given in CH-1903 format. The coordinates of the block point clouds are kept in a lokal x/y/z coordinate system.", "doi": "10.3390/geosciences8030088", "format": "ascii x, y, z", "hash": "", "id": "8cf275ca-06d0-47cf-b67f-48780b019ae6", "last_modified": "2019-01-07T11:58:54.985810", "metadata_modified": "2022-02-16T15:44:28.290736", "mimetype": "application/zip", "mimetype_inner": null, "name": "Tschamut2014_Slope+BlockScans", "package_id": "6a7664a6-77a9-49c9-9498-4b63c018fa09", "position": 0, "resource_size": "", "resource_type": null, "restricted": "{\"level\": \"public\", \"allowed_users\": \"\"}", "size": 1779331, "state": "active", "url": "https://www.envidat.ch/dataset/6a7664a6-77a9-49c9-9498-4b63c018fa09/resource/8cf275ca-06d0-47cf-b67f-48780b019ae6/download/geosciences-08-00088-s001.zip", "url_type": "upload"}, {"cache_last_updated": null, "cache_url": null, "created": "2022-02-16T15:44:28.321535", "description": "This table gives an overview on all tests performed including\r\n- block used\r\n- start & end position\r\n- number of jumps\r\n- etc.\r\n- ", "doi": "", "format": "ZIP", "hash": "", "id": "467dc8f8-9069-4c87-8856-3d12817633be", "last_modified": null, "metadata_modified": "2022-02-16T16:04:27.550546", "mimetype": null, "mimetype_inner": null, "name": "Overview of all tests", "package_id": "6a7664a6-77a9-49c9-9498-4b63c018fa09", "position": 1, "publication_state": "", "resource_size": "{\"size_units\": \"kb\", \"size_value\": \"\"}", "resource_type": null, "restricted": "{\"level\": \"public\", \"allowed_users\": \"\"}", "size": 44962, "state": "active", "url": "https://www.envidat.ch/dataset/6a7664a6-77a9-49c9-9498-4b63c018fa09/resource/467dc8f8-9069-4c87-8856-3d12817633be/download/overviewalltests.zip", "url_type": "upload"}, {"cache_last_updated": null, "cache_url": null, "created": "2022-02-16T15:52:53.881083", "description": "This file contains more than 80 rockfall trajectories projected onto the terrain, i.e. the positions of the single blocks over time during the single tests that were recorded by the local positioning system with about 10Hz. It contains the detected positions as well as a smoothened path (see Volkwein et al., Geosciences, 2018). The table also contains the derived velocities and accelerations along the slope (attention: these accelerations are the once that occur during an impact).", "doi": "", "format": "ascii, tab separated, also as Excel table", "hash": "", "id": "b6dc0f14-5b86-4353-a2a6-ef06c0ddf0ad", "last_modified": "2022-02-16T17:05:31.457407", "metadata_modified": "2022-02-16T16:19:35.691131", "mimetype": null, "mimetype_inner": null, "name": "Block trajectories recorded from local positioning system", "package_id": "6a7664a6-77a9-49c9-9498-4b63c018fa09", "position": 2, "publication_state": "", "resource_size": "{\"size_units\": \"kb\", \"size_value\": \"\"}", "resource_type": null, "restricted": "{\"level\": \"public\", \"allowed_users\": \"\"}", "size": 6430962, "state": "active", "url": "https://www.envidat.ch/dataset/6a7664a6-77a9-49c9-9498-4b63c018fa09/resource/b6dc0f14-5b86-4353-a2a6-ef06c0ddf0ad/download/trajectoriesfromlps.zip", "url_type": "upload"}, {"cache_last_updated": null, "cache_url": null, "created": "2022-02-16T15:58:09.961683", "description": "This table contains data of more than 2200 of each jumps and impacts of the test blocks on a grassy slope. It gives there durations in combination with acting accerlartions and the rotational speed of the blocks. The data were retrieved using the block internal accelerometer and rotation sensors. The combination of these data with the measurement from the local positioning system allows the deduction of jump lengths, slope gradient etc.", "doi": "", "format": "ascii, tab separated, also as excel table", "hash": "", "id": "e2f0958e-2b51-49ce-ba25-40c4ffd331a7", "last_modified": "2022-02-16T16:59:12.631818", "metadata_modified": "2022-02-16T15:59:13.171533", "mimetype": null, "mimetype_inner": null, "name": "Jumps and impacts", "package_id": "6a7664a6-77a9-49c9-9498-4b63c018fa09", "position": 3, "publication_state": "", "resource_size": "{\"size_value\": \"\", \"size_units\": \"kb\"}", "resource_type": null, "restricted": "{\"level\": \"public\", \"allowed_users\": \"\"}", "size": 1051503, "state": "active", "url": "https://www.envidat.ch/dataset/6a7664a6-77a9-49c9-9498-4b63c018fa09/resource/e2f0958e-2b51-49ce-ba25-40c4ffd331a7/download/jumpsandimpacts.zip", "url_type": "upload"}], "tags": [{"display_name": "EXPERIMENT", "id": "387726dc-dbe2-4c70-bdf1-414144a5ed04", "name": "EXPERIMENT", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}, {"display_name": "EXPERIMENTS", "id": "ba58e6e2-eb93-4647-ba1e-b15f1229880d", "name": "EXPERIMENTS", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}, {"display_name": "FIELD DATA", "id": "2eb3e96f-b26e-43be-9448-a64ba3b0e848", "name": "FIELD DATA", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}, {"display_name": "FIELD TEST", "id": "afd0d300-68f1-4aac-ab86-d1caa6e45e2f", "name": "FIELD TEST", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}, {"display_name": "FIELD TESTS", "id": "bc8b1692-4e93-4ca3-80a9-55c04265dfd7", "name": "FIELD TESTS", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}, {"display_name": "MASS MOVEMENTS", "id": "83ed54e7-428d-4ed5-9d7c-d168dc60895d", "name": "MASS MOVEMENTS", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}, {"display_name": "NATURAL HAZARDS", "id": "b4f09b99-ea70-452b-b22a-8be9d8961b57", "name": "NATURAL HAZARDS", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}, {"display_name": "ROCKFALL", "id": "9097352d-c506-4009-9642-6a2991cf4a7d", "name": "ROCKFALL", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}, {"display_name": "TRAJECTORY", "id": "7b76f175-72b1-4fa3-9f00-7fb19dde2ea2", "name": "TRAJECTORY", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}], "groups": [], "relationships_as_subject": [], "relationships_as_object": []}}